  "comparison": {
    "baseline_3lf": {"macro_f1": 0.5298, "f1_stag": 0.1513, "f1_prog": 0.9082},
    "no_cmdrep": {"macro_f1": 0.4883, "f1_stag": 0.6246, "f1_prog": 0.3520},
    "delta": -0.0415
  },
  "analysis": "Removing cmd_rep causes massive label distribution shift on both sides. SWE goes from progress-heavy to 40/60 stag/prog. OH flips from 93% progress to 55% stagnation. The probe learns different decision boundaries under the new label regime, and the distribution mismatch between SWE (40% stag) and OH (55% stag) no-cmdrep labels hurts transfer. The f1_stag improved dramatically (0.15→0.62) but f1_prog collapsed (0.91→0.35), suggesting the no-cmdrep probe is biased toward stagnation prediction."
